        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/ed8c4c/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-04-06T00:46:32.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hey All,</p><p>I attended PAX East and watched the tournament there and had a question. In a game that is so easily deliniated by turns and rounds, why do they use an overall game time instead of round timing or a Chess Clock style game? It seems like a team could make an abusive build that would get an early kill and bunker/heal and then chew time until the win. Are there rules in place to prevent this? I will be at Gencon and it just seems like something that you'd want to avoid.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:44:26.323Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
