        "raw": "<p>Hey All,</p><p>I attended PAX East and watched the tournament there and had a question. In a game that is so easily deliniated by turns and rounds, why do they use an overall game time instead of round timing or a Chess Clock style game? It seems like a team could make an abusive build that would get an early kill and bunker/heal and then chew time until the win. Are there rules in place to prevent this? I will be at Gencon and it just seems like something that you&#39;d want to avoid.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
